course: dictionary
lesson: 3141
title: Elsewhere: somewhere else
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Elsewhere is an adverb. It means in or to another place, somewhere else. When you meet it, ask yourself: is the thing here, or is it in a different place?
explain: «Walk in the kitchen and play elsewhere while cooking happens.» The kitchen is where the cooking is, so elsewhere means somewhere away from the kitchen. Try your meaning in the sentence: "play somewhere else while cooking happens" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Elsewhere can also compare places. «It was the same story elsewhere.» means the same thing happened in other places too. Look at the words around it to find the other place the author is thinking of.
fact: Elsewhere means in or to another place, somewhere else.
fact: «Look elsewhere» means search in a different place when you cannot find something.
fact: «In Japan, and in many homes elsewhere, people take their shoes off at the door.» Here elsewhere means in many other homes, not only in Japan.
fact: «It was the same story elsewhere.» means the same thing happened in other places too.
fact: Here and elsewhere means in this place and in other places.
exercise: «I can't find my pencil here, so I will look elsewhere.» What does elsewhere mean here? | Never at all | *In another place | In this same place | Under the table, right next to me
exercise: «Walk in the kitchen and play elsewhere while cooking happens.» Where should the child play? | Right in the kitchen, in the middle of the cooking | *In a different room, away from the cooking | On the kitchen table | Inside the oven
exercise: «It was the same story elsewhere.» Find and copy the word that means in another place. | same | story | was | *elsewhere
test: «In Japan, and in many homes elsewhere, people take their shoes off at the door.» What does elsewhere mean? | Only in the hallway at the door | Upstairs in bed | *In other homes and places, not only in Japan | In the kitchen, while cooking
test: Which word means the same as elsewhere? | *somewhere else | nowhere | everywhere | right here
exam: Mia says, «Let's go elsewhere, this park is too busy.» What does she want? | To go nowhere at all | To stay in this busy park | To go home and sleep | *To go to a different place
